<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<usx version="3.0">
  <book code="2TH" style="id">2 THESSALONIANS</book>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="2TH 1"/>
  <para style="s1">Apostolic Greeting</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="2TH 1:1"/>
    Paul, Silvanus, and Timothy,
    <verse eid="2TH 1:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">To the church of the Thessalonians who live in God our Father and in the Lord Jesus Christ.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="2TH 1:2"/>
    May grace or unmerited favour and peace be given to you from God the Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.
    <verse eid="2TH 1:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Giving Thanks to God on Behalf of the Saints</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="2TH 1:3"/>
    We are continually obligated to thank God for you, brothers and sisters, as is entirely appropriate, because your faith is advancing remarkably and the love each one of you has for one another is steadily increasing.
    <verse eid="2TH 1:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="2TH 1:4"/>
    As a result, we ourselves speak with pride about you among the churches of God, because of your steadfast endurance and faith in the midst of all the persecutions and hardships that you are continuing to bear.
    <verse eid="2TH 1:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Eschatological Judgment and Glory</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="2TH 1:5"/>
    All of this serves as clear evidence of the righteous judgment of God, demonstrating that you will be regarded as worthy of the kingdom of God, for which you are now suffering.
    <verse eid="2TH 1:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="2TH 1:6"/>
    For it is right and just for God to repay distress to those who are causing you distress,
    <verse eid="2TH 1:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="2TH 1:7"/>
    and to grant relief to you who are being afflicted, along with us, when the Lord Jesus is revealed from heaven with His powerful angels,
    <verse eid="2TH 1:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="2TH 1:8"/>
    appearing in blazing fire to execute righteous judgment on those who do not know God and on those who refuse to obey the gospel of our Lord Jesus.
    <verse eid="2TH 1:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="2TH 1:9"/>
    Such people will suffer the penalty of everlasting ruin, separated from the presence of the Lord and from the manifestation of His majestic power,
    <verse eid="2TH 1:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="2TH 1:10"/>
    when He comes on that day to be glorified among His saints and to be marvelled at among all who have believed, because the testimony we delivered to you was accepted as true.
    <verse eid="2TH 1:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Pauline Prayer</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="2TH 1:11"/>
    With this goal in view, we always pray for you, that our God may regard you as worthy of His calling and may bring to full completion every resolve for goodness and every work produced by faith through His power,
    <verse eid="2TH 1:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="2TH 1:12"/>
    so that the name of our Lord Jesus may be honoured in you, and you in Him, according to the grace of our God and the Lord Jesus Christ.
    <verse eid="2TH 1:12"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="2TH 1"/>
  <chapter number="2" style="c" sid="2TH 2"/>
  <para style="s1">The Revelation of the Man of Lawlessness</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="2TH 2:1"/>
    Now we appeal to you, brothers and sisters, regarding the return of our Lord Jesus Christ and our being gathered to Him,
    <verse eid="2TH 2:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="2TH 2:2"/>
    that you not be easily unsettled in your thinking or thrown into fear, whether by a spiritual claim, by a spoken message, or by a letter alleged to come from us, asserting that the day of the Lord has already arrived.
    <verse eid="2TH 2:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="2TH 2:3"/>
    Do not allow anyone to mislead you in any manner, because that day will not occur unless the rebellion comes first and the man of lawlessness is unveiled, the one destined for destruction,
    <verse eid="2TH 2:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="2TH 2:4"/>
    who sets himself in opposition and elevates himself above every so-called god or object of worship, to the point that he instals himself in the sanctuary of God, publicly presenting himself as God.
    <verse eid="2TH 2:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="2TH 2:5"/>
    Do you not remember that I repeatedly spoke about these matters while I was still with you?
    <verse eid="2TH 2:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="2TH 2:6"/>
    And now you know what is presently restraining him, so that he will be revealed at the appointed time.
    <verse eid="2TH 2:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="2TH 2:7"/>
    For the hidden force of lawlessness is already at work; only the One who restrains it now will continue to do so until He is removed from the way.
    <verse eid="2TH 2:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="2TH 2:8"/>
    Then the lawless one will be openly revealed, whom the Lord will destroy by the breath of His mouth and render powerless by the splendour of His appearing.
    <verse eid="2TH 2:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="2TH 2:9"/>
    The coming of this one is in accordance with the activity of Satan, accompanied by every kind of counterfeit power, signs, and deceptive wonders,
    <verse eid="2TH 2:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="2TH 2:10"/>
    and by every form of wicked deception directed towards those who are perishing, because they refused to welcome the love of the truth that would have brought them salvation.
    <verse eid="2TH 2:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="2TH 2:11"/>
    For this reason, God sends upon them a powerful delusion, so that they will embrace what is false,
    <verse eid="2TH 2:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="2TH 2:12"/>
    in order that all may be judged who did not believe the truth, but took pleasure in unrighteousness.
    <verse eid="2TH 2:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Giving Thanks to God</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="2TH 2:13"/>
    But we must always thank God for you, brothers and sisters loved by the Lord, because from the beginning God chose you for salvation through sanctification by the Spirit and faith in the truth.
    <verse eid="2TH 2:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="2TH 2:14"/>
    It was for this very purpose that He called you through our gospel, so that you might share in the glory of our Lord Jesus Christ.
    <verse eid="2TH 2:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Encouragement to Stand Resolute</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="2TH 2:15"/>
    Therefore, brothers and sisters, stand firm and hold tightly to the teachings you were instructed in, whether conveyed by spoken message or by a letter from us.
    <verse eid="2TH 2:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Pauline Prayer</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="2TH 2:16"/>
    Now may our Lord Jesus Christ Himself, and God our Father, who loved us and graciously granted us eternal encouragement and a good hope,
    <verse eid="2TH 2:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="2TH 2:17"/>
    strengthen your hearts and establish you in every good deed and word.
    <verse eid="2TH 2:17"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="2TH 2"/>
  <chapter number="3" style="c" sid="2TH 3"/>
  <para style="s1">Paul’s Appeal for Prayer</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="2TH 3:1"/>
    Finally, brothers and sisters, pray for us, so that the message of the Lord may spread rapidly and be honoured, just as it was among you,
    <verse eid="2TH 3:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="2TH 3:2"/>
    and that we may be rescued from corrupt and wicked people, for faith is not possessed by everyone.
    <verse eid="2TH 3:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="2TH 3:3"/>
    But the Lord is faithful; He will strengthen you and protect you from the evil one.
    <verse eid="2TH 3:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="2TH 3:4"/>
    We have confidence in the Lord concerning you, that you are practising and will continue to practise the things we instruct you to do.
    <verse eid="2TH 3:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Pauline Prayer</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="2TH 3:5"/>
    May the Lord guide your hearts into the love of God and into steadfast endurance shaped by Christ.
    <verse eid="2TH 3:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Warning Against Idleness</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="2TH 3:6"/>
    Now we command you, brothers and sisters, in the name of our Lord Jesus Christ, to withdraw from every brother who lives in a disorderly manner and not in accordance with the teaching they received from us.
    <verse eid="2TH 3:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="2TH 3:7"/>
    For you yourselves know how you ought to follow our example, because we did not live irresponsibly while we were among you,
    <verse eid="2TH 3:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="2TH 3:8"/>
    nor did we accept food from anyone without payment, but with exhausting labour we worked day and night, so that we would not place a burden on any of you.
    <verse eid="2TH 3:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="2TH 3:9"/>
    This was not because we lacked the right to such support, but in order to present ourselves as a pattern for you to imitate.
    <verse eid="2TH 3:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="2TH 3:10"/>
    Even while we were with you, we repeatedly gave this instruction: If anyone is unwilling to work, that person should not eat.
    <verse eid="2TH 3:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="2TH 3:11"/>
    For we hear that some among you are living irresponsibly, not working at all, but interfering in matters that do not concern them.
    <verse eid="2TH 3:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="2TH 3:12"/>
    Such people we command and urge in the Lord Jesus Christ to work quietly and earn the food they themselves eat.
    <verse eid="2TH 3:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="2TH 3:13"/>
    But you, brothers and sisters, do not lose heart in doing what is good.
    <verse eid="2TH 3:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="2TH 3:14"/>
    If anyone does not obey our instruction in this letter, take note of that person and do not associate closely with him, so that he may feel the seriousness of his conduct.
    <verse eid="2TH 3:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="2TH 3:15"/>
    Yet do not treat him as an enemy, but warn him as a brother.
    <verse eid="2TH 3:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Pauline Prayer</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="2TH 3:16"/>
    Now may the Lord of peace Himself grant you peace at all times and in every circumstance. The Lord be with you all.
    <verse eid="2TH 3:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Greeting</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="2TH 3:17"/>
    I, Paul, write this greeting with my own hand, which serves as a mark of authenticity in every letter. This is how I write.
    <verse eid="2TH 3:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="2TH 3:18"/>
    May the grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with all of you.
    <verse eid="2TH 3:18"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="2TH 3"/>
</usx>
